# Admin dashboard dark mode

When touching admin UI (`/admin`, `admin-neu`, admin Tailwind/CSS), **ship dark mode with light mode**. Do not leave new surfaces light-only.

## Source of truth

- Theme tokens live as CSS vars on `.skoun-admin` / `.skoun-admin[data-theme="dark"]` in `frontend/styles/admin.input.css`.
- Tailwind `clay` / `moss` / `ember` / `ochre` + `shadow-neu*` read those vars (`frontend/tailwind.config.js`).
- Toggle + persist: `AdminNeuShell` + `components/admin-neu/theme.ts` (`skoun-admin-theme`).
- After token/class changes: `npm run admin:css` in `frontend`.

## Rules

1. Prefer Tailwind tokens (`bg-clay-100`, `text-clay-900`, `shadow-neu`, `text-moss`) — they flip automatically.
2. No hardcoded hex for admin UI (`#E4E9F0`, `#8A96A6`, `#2F6B63`, etc.). Use classes or `ADMIN_MUTED` / `ADMIN_CHART` from `theme.ts`.
3. Lucide muted icons: `color={ADMIN_MUTED}` (CSS `var(--admin-clay-500)`).
4. Charts/SVG strokes/fills: `ADMIN_CHART.*` or CSS vars — never fixed light-only hex.
5. Overlays/scrims: `.admin-scrim` (not `bg-clay-900/20` — clay-900 is text ink and flips).
6. New accents: add light + dark vars in `admin.input.css`, wire through Tailwind if reusable.
7. Keep neumorphism: extruded (`shadow-neu*`) and inset (`shadow-neu-in*`, `shadow-press`) must stay visible in both themes.
8. Check contrast for `text-clay-500` / `700` on dark surfaces; bump if muddy.
9. Date inputs / form controls inherit `color-scheme` from root — do not force light chrome.

## Quick check

- [ ] Toggle dark in shell; new UI matches clay surface + neu shadows
- [ ] Icons/charts not stuck on light hex
- [ ] `admin:css` rebuilt if tokens or class names changed
